@eliebakouch took a second look at a viral model and found that it is a direct copy of Nemotron 3 Nano, sharing about 80% of its architecture and training data, which overemphasizes its sovereign aspect. The main issue is that the model was trained on benchmark evaluation sets, including GPQA Diamond, which accounts for 20% of its capability score and explains about 70% of the performance gap with Nemotron Nano.

Furthermore, the dataset used for training, AIML-TUDA/QA-base, is a very light rephrasing of the GPQA Diamond test set, raising concerns about data contamination and overfitting on test data.

I really like BFL folks, so I am pretty happy to see this progress from them.

